_________________________________
ruining code:

run the demo by doing this:
uv run demo.py

this will load the model and classify text given in the command line
---------------------------------
other nots:
we can get data from a pipeline 
this pipeline is the data_pipe_extract_features.py

and example of the useing this is 
cat AI_text/meta1.txt | uv run data_pipe_extract_features.py -AI -schema -pipe > data.csv

this will pipe the data into a csv 
the -schema will print the schema for the csv so if you would like to append to this we can do this

cat  -s <AI_text_file_name.txt>| uv run data_pipe_extract_features.py -AI -pipe >> data.csv
or
cat -s <human_text_file_name.txt>| uv run data_pipe_extract_features.py -human -pipe >> data.csv


we can now chuck the data 
for example if we chunk the data into 500 peases we get 

cat  -s human_text/* | uv run data_pipe_extract_features.py -human -pipe -schema -S 500 > data.csv

the -S is the size of the chunks---------------------------------------------------^

i did cut the future of word count because i didn't want the model to think that the uniform number = human 

-------

so we added a bunch of stuff

extract_and_append_ai_data.py - takes AI data from batch CSVs and pipes through the feature extraction 
process_hf_dataset.py - downloads the huggingface dataset and pipes each row through the pipeline
download_hf_dataset.py - just downloads and shows you the dataset from huggingface

the data.csv now has 1996 samples (998 human texts, 998 AI texts from 6 different models - gemma, mistral, qwen, llama, yi, gpt4o)

we extract 41 features from each text:
- sentence length stuff (avg and variance)
- vocab metrics (density, hapax ratio, type token ratio)
- word length analysis 
- punctuation counts for like 32 different punctuation marks
- stopword count

if you want to run the huggingface script again just know it appends to data.csv so you'll get duplicates if you run it twice
we already have all the data loaded so don't run it again unless you want more

